Confirmed the bug. yoyo setup runs the wizard (which saves .yoyo.toml with provider=openrouter) then returns `Some(None)` = exits the process. When the user next runs yoyo and types "hi":
• .yoyo.toml now exists → needs_setup() returns false → wizard doesn't re-run
• The api_key was never persisted (config stores only provider/model/base_url), and the env var set during the wizard died with that process
• So the OpenRouter key is gone → yoyo falls back to trying Anthropic → 401

The core defect: **the API key entered during the wizard is not persisted anywhere durable.** The wizard's own hint even says "or set ENV in your shell" — so it assumes the key lives in the environment, but a user who types the key directly loses it. This is a genuine product bug affecting every non-env-var user.

Let me check whether .yoyo.toml supports an api_key key at load time, to know if persisting it is even possible.
